  "live_records": {
    "q-93064": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93064",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The following table shows the width and length,  in meters, of a rectangular agriculture field.\n\n| Width | Length |\n| --- | --- |\n| $667$ | $1\\,432$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of width to length for this field.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the width and length by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- width: $667⟶700$\n\n- length: $1\\,432⟶1\\,400$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of width to length is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{700}{1\\,400}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{700÷100}{1\\,400÷100}=\\frac{7}{14}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7÷7}{14÷7}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of width to length is approximately $\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
